# Purpose

This source package is based on the upstream opentelemetry-collector git tree
but is only used to build the builder.  This is the tool which we then use
the build a custom opentelemetry builder for PexOS.

# Vendoring for a new upstream

In order to build offline we need to vendor the dependencies properly.  To
do this, import the new orig into the upstream-${suite} branch and delete
the contents of cmd/builder/vendor.

Working on the upstream-{suite} branch, use `cd cmd/builder/vendor && go mod
vendor` (ensuring that the right version of go is on your path) to vendor the
files in cmd/builder/vendor, then move them to the top level

```
export PATH=/usr/lib/go-1.26/bin:${PATH}
export GOTOOLCHAIN=local
cd cmd/builder/vendor && go mod vendor && mv vendor ../../buildervendor
```

Commit the buildervendor directory to the upstream branch.

Tar the directory up (from the repo dir):

```
tar -zcvf ../opentelemetry-collector-builder_${version}.orig-buildervendor.tar.gz buildervendor/
```

Then add the extra tarball to pristine-tar:

```
pristine-tar commit ../opentelemetry-collector-builder_${version}.orig-buildervendor.tar.gz upstream-${suite}
```

Push the upstream and pristine-tar branches and update the Pexip branches as
usual.
